# Stakeholder / Telegram messages (An preference — fossil)

When drafting messages to humans outside the IDE (Telegram, WhatsApp, email-to-stakeholder, “what should I send”):

- Very short. Condensed. Caveman-clear.
- Human and polite. Kind, sincere. A few small typos or oddities OK if it still reads natural.
- No em dashes (—). Use commas, full stops, or "to" / "and".
- Almost all prose paragraphs. Few or no bullet points.
- Cover the point once (need, cost, time, users, maintenance, next hoop if relevant). Then stop.
- No jargon dumps. No pressure. Soft close (thanks / happy to chat).

Do not use this voice for code, commits, or in-IDE teaching (keep teach-an for those).
